# Cloudinary Patterns

## ⛔ Hard rule: namespace
**Every Cloudinary asset for this project MUST live under `sofi-mosquera/`.**
The cloud `dsrvlln9j` is shared with other projects (`suplement-app/`,
`zapata-goma/`, `underfeet/`). Mixing assets across folders breaks the audit
trail and can collide with other apps' DB references.

Exported helpers from `@sofi/ui`:
- `SOFI_NAMESPACE` = `"sofi-mosquera"`
- `assertSofiPath(value, ctx?)` → throws if value is not under namespace.
  Use it in any code path that constructs or stores a public_id.
- `isSofiPath(value)` → boolean version.

## Sub-folder convention (canonical)
```
sofi-mosquera/projects/{slug}/{01..NN}
sofi-mosquera/artworks/{seriesSlug}/{slug}/cover   (series-grouped)
sofi-mosquera/artworks/{slug}/cover                (no series)
sofi-mosquera/artworks/{slug}/context              (installation/context shot)
sofi-mosquera/furniture/{slug}/{01..NN}
sofi-mosquera/about/sofia-{01..03}
sofi-mosquera/branding/{sm-dark|sm-white|wordmark-dark|wordmark-white}
```

## DB convention
- Store **public_id** in `cover_url`, `context_url`, `gallery[]`. NEVER full URLs.
- Use the `video:` prefix only to mark a public_id whose source is a video
  (rendered via `BASE_VIDEO/.../so_auto/{id}` to extract a poster frame).

## URL building — always use helpers
```tsx
import { cldCard, cldHero, cldGallery } from "@sofi/ui";

<img src={cldCard(project.coverUrl)} alt="..." />
```

Available presets:
- `cldUrl(publicId, opts)` — generic
- `cldThumb` — 600×750 fill 4:5
- `cldCard` — 800×1000 fill 4:5
- `cldHero` — 2000×1200 wide
- `cldSquare` — 600×600
- `cldArtwork` — 900×1200 fit (preserves aspect)
- `cldGallery` — 1600×1000 fill detail
- `cldZoom` — 2400 limit, q90 lightbox
- `cldEnhanced` / `cldUpscaled` / `cldPortrait` — AI variants

## Upload workflow (and how to NOT break the namespace)
- Bulk from filesystem: `npx tsx scripts/upload-images.ts`
  → script asserts `publicId.startsWith("sofi-mosquera/")` before uploading.
- Branding/logos: `npx tsx scripts/upload-branding.ts`
  → same guard.
- Admin UI: `<CloudinaryUpload>` defaults to `folder="sofi-mosquera"` and
  `/api/cloudinary-sign` rejects any `paramsToSign` that points outside.
- Manual rename of misplaced assets: write a one-off script using
  `cloudinary.uploader.rename(from, to, { invalidate: true })` —
  see `scripts/rename-emociones-assets.ts` for the template.

## Cache busting
- Every URL carries `vNNNNNNNN` (hardcoded `ASSET_VERSION` in
  `packages/ui/src/lib/cloudinary.ts`). Bump it whenever assets are
  re-uploaded at the same public_id, or the CDN may serve stale 404s for
  several minutes after a rename.

## Audit / verification
- `npx tsx scripts/audit-cloudinary.ts` — full inventory grouped by folder.
- `pnpm --filter @sofi/db exec tsx audit-db-vs-cloudinary.ts` — cross-checks
  every DB cover_url/gallery against the Cloudinary inventory. Should be
  green at all times.
